# Challenges Faced

## 1. Nested Project Directory

### Problem

After extracting the Spring Boot project, the directory structure became:

```text
devops_project/
└── Task_Manager/
    └── Task_Manager/
        ├── pom.xml
        ├── src/
        └── ...
```

The actual project was nested one level deeper than intended.

### Root Cause

The ZIP archive was extracted into a folder that had the same name as the project, resulting in an additional directory level.

### Resolution

Moved the project contents to the correct location so the final structure became:

```text
Task_Manager/
├── pom.xml
├── src/
├── .mvn/
├── mvnw
└── ...
```

### Lesson Learned

Always verify the project structure immediately after extracting downloaded archives.

The project root should directly contain:

- `pom.xml`
- `src/`
- `.mvn/`
- `mvnw`

---

## 2. Windows Zone.Identifier Files

### Problem

Several unexpected files appeared, including:

```text
pom.xml:Zone.Identifier
mvnw:Zone.Identifier
HELP.md:Zone.Identifier
```

### Root Cause

Windows automatically attaches alternate data streams (`Zone.Identifier`) to downloaded files to indicate they originated from the Internet. When accessed through WSL, these appeared as regular files.

### Resolution

Removed all metadata files using:

```bash
find . -name "*:Zone.Identifier" -delete
```

### Lesson Learned

These files are not part of the application source code and should never be committed to Git.

---

## 3. Git Repository Placement

### Problem

Git was initially initialized outside the actual Spring Boot project.

```text
devops_project/
├── .git
└── Task_Manager/
```

### Why It Matters

This configuration would track unrelated files such as ZIP archives and other directories, making the repository harder to maintain.

### Resolution

Initialized Git inside the project root.

Final structure:

```text
Task_Manager/
├── .git/
├── pom.xml
├── src/
└── ...
```

### Lesson Learned

A Git repository should usually be initialized at the root of a single project.

---

## 4. Duplicate README Files

### Problem

The repository contained:

```text
README
README.md
```

### Resolution

Removed the duplicate `README` file and retained `README.md`.

### Lesson Learned

GitHub automatically renders `README.md`.

Maintaining only one README avoids confusion.

---

## 5. Unnecessary ZIP Archive

### Problem

The repository still contained the downloaded ZIP archive after extraction.

### Resolution

Deleted the archive after verifying the extracted project.

### Lesson Learned

Repositories should contain only source code and project-related files.

Temporary downloads and archives should not be committed.

